{"annotationDigest":"sha256:0ebb82dab4e9a0d6d4a77a8afdb4158124eb4e71306e1b5c6d0087563393af85","annotationId":"rann-c75059bfd9b442720d692c681241f8d4","author":{"agent":"claude-code","kind":"ai","model":"claude-opus-5.5"},"createdAt":"2026-10-01T23:32:04Z","disclaimer":"AI-generated review opinion derived from the evidence package. It is not a verdict, does not change readiness, and must be confirmed by a human reviewer.","disclosureCheck":{"blocking":29,"contradictions":[],"disclosures":31,"nextDecision":"human_judgement","readiness":"not_assessed"},"findings":[{"claim":{"params":{"requirement":"SW-REQ-260925-XTGG"},"type":"requirement_affected"},"detail":"`if (root.requestActive) root.finishRequest(null)` at the top of open() (Menu.qml:33) runs before openDmenu()/openRoute() overwrite or clear selectionFile/doneFile/requestActive. finishRequest captures the old done-file path, clears the request and writes `: > <doneFile>`, so the superseded bin/omarchy-menu-select caller (poll loop at bin/omarchy-menu-select:93) exits 1 as on Escape. Fixes #9057. XTGG is our proof work codifying it; head b7bd59c4 keeps the guard unchanged.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":33},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":130},{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-select","kind":"file","line":93},{"id":"SW-REQ-260925-XTGG","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"info","title":"Upstream 0b4fe292: open() answers an in-flight select/input request as cancelled before the next summon (SW-REQ-260925-XTGG)","verification":{"evidence":[{"id":"SW-REQ-260925-XTGG","kind":"requirement"}],"method":"review.changes (spec, code-trace, function and call-level requirement impact)","note":"SW-REQ-260925-XTGG is in review.changes (added, matchLevel file).","status":"confirmed"}},{"claim":{"params":{"requirement":"SW-REQ-261001-C19S"},"type":"requirement_affected"},"detail":"finishRequest now calls Quickshell.execDetached for the cancel write and for the selection write (Menu.qml:146, 148) instead of setting command/running on the shared resultProc. A Process ignores running = true while it still runs, so on 0b4fe292 an answer issued during an earlier write was dropped and its caller polled forever. Copilot flagged this shared-Process race on 2026-08-30; @omarchybot reproduced the burst and pushed b7bd59c4. The resultProc Process, its onExited and the requestSerial/applySerial counters that only fed it are removed. SW-REQ-261001-C19S (our proof work) states the rule; the reviewer's live burst outside this package (20 concurrent omarchy-menu-select): 19/20 callers stuck on quattro, 7-12/20 on 0b4fe292, 0/20 on b7bd59c4 and on b7bd59c4 merged onto c05d9019.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":146},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":148},{"id":"SW-REQ-261001-C19S","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"info","title":"Upstream b7bd59c4 (@omarchybot): every answer is written by a process of its own (SW-REQ-261001-C19S)","verification":{"evidence":[{"id":"SW-REQ-261001-C19S","kind":"requirement"}],"method":"review.changes (spec, code-trace, function and call-level requirement impact)","note":"SW-REQ-261001-C19S is in review.changes (added, matchLevel file).","status":"confirmed"}},{"claim":{"params":{"requirement":"SW-REQ-260922-FGZQ"},"type":"requirement_affected"},"detail":"The removed onExited set opened = false after the write, if no newer request had started. Every apply path already sets opened = false itself before it calls finishRequest (applyDmenuSelection, applySelected, the app-launch row, cancel), on the baseline and on b7bd59c4 alike, so the re-close was redundant. Reviewer behaviour-diff harness outside this package (real Menu.qml bodies under node vm, 86,463 event sequences per pair): 2 intended differences (superseded caller cancelled; answer during a busy write now written), 0 unintended, no state/action/app-launch/double-write differences. REVIEW-50 was re-read on b7bd59c4; FGZQ's text is unchanged.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":884},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":130},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-FGZQ","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"info","title":"Removing resultProc.onExited does not change when the menu closes (SW-REQ-260922-FGZQ)","verification":{"evidence":[{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-FGZQ","kind":"requirement"}],"method":"review.changes (spec, code-trace, function and call-level requirement impact)","note":"SW-REQ-260922-FGZQ is in review.changes (code_changed, matchLevel file).","status":"confirmed"}},{"claim":{"params":{"requirement":"SW-REQ-260922-50RE"},"type":"requirement_affected"},"detail":"Any Menu.qml edit stales every file-level trace link to it, so the 30 Menu.qml-linked requirements were re-reviewed with citations (proof trace review --citation), and menu-test.sh is traced to many more at file level. Their clauses and FRETish are unchanged. The impact sidecar proof/impact-reviews/pr-9056.yaml records no-authored-change for the 7 shared-ownership requirements. Our proof work, not upstream.","refs":[{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-3JG5","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-3T3F","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-3VTN","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-4079","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-46HY","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-50RE","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-74BZ","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-7NPE","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-8CQ4","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-B757","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-C8HX","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-CYB9","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-DE93","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-DQ9P","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-E4J2","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-EFNR","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-JRW1","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-N3RM","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-