in this PR's scope)","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Peer-death: bounded wait in omarchy-menu-select\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"detail":"The project behaviour-diff harness (test/bdiff, 213 inputs over 5 partitions) records 16 differences between quattro-proof 9f3abc10 and the evaluated tree. The reviewer re-ran the harness at both revisions for each input: 14 are superseded callers going from STRANDED to <cancel> (2-caller sequences, and bursts of 20 and 22 where 19 or 21 callers move), classified intended against SW-REQ-260925-XTGG; 2 (SASP, lifecycle and timing) are an answer issued while the earlier cancel write still runs going from STRANDED to the value 'alpha', classified intended against SW-REQ-261001-C19S. In no input does a head caller stay STRANDED, and no final state, action, app launch or stray write differs. The removed-behaviour inventory is empty (the engine does not inventory the removed QML Process/onExited/serials; bdiff/9056.md did that by hand). Two more findings: cf-fed95cab816ff9a6 is the intended flip of the #9057 report test, and cf-c8dd4255b9f5771b says the B8N9 witness Menu.qml:233:item is gone, but item(id) only moved to line 243 and proof mcdc show still lists it (a line-keyed identity question for the engine). Each needs a reviewer's accept_compat_change; this review does not approve anything.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":243},{"id":"SW-REQ-260929-B8N9","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260925-XTGG","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-261001-C19S","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"test/node/report-reproducers.test.mjs","kind":"file","line":62}],"severity":"medium","title":"18 compatibility findings await a reviewer; the 16 behaviour differences are classified intended","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"claim":{"params":{"path":"test/reports/report-cmulr95nw0kqr1gw46i7f50xj.sh","position":"noise"},"type":"unmapped_code"},"detail":"test/reports/report-cmulr95nw0kqr1gw46i7f50xj.sh extracts the real Menu.qml request functions; without a Quickshell.execDetached stub it stops with SETUP (rc 2) on b7bd59c4 (ReferenceError). The added stub runs the command with bash, like the resultProc stub. Test harness, no product behaviour.","refs":[{"id":"test/reports/report-cmulr95nw0kqr1gw46i7f50xj.sh","kind":"file","line":92}],"severity":"info","title":"Unmapped: the #9057 report script's stub scope now also runs execDetached commands","verification":{"evidence":[{"id":"test/reports/report-cmulr95nw0kqr1gw46i7f50xj.sh","kind":"file"}],"method":"review.scope (changed units, intent graph, spec-gap candidates): units","note":"test/reports/report-cmulr95nw0kqr1gw46i7f50xj.sh (modified) is traced to no requirement. The author's position (noise) is judgement, not verified; a human decision settles it.","status":"confirmed"}},{"detail":"review.effects is absent (effects_unavailable), so call-path statements here come from reading the code. The behaviour-diff harness replays the real Menu.qml request functions under node:vm, which covers the request lifecycle but not Quickshell's own process spawning.","refs":[{"id":"review.effects.approximations","kind":"check"},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":22}],"severity":"info","title":"Analysis bounds: no change-effects analysis for QML","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"Evaluated tree c0a4a030 = baseline quattro-proof 9f3abc10 (upstream f45461a3; Menu.qml identical to 4f1a8197) + the full upstream diff 158e8cfb..b7bd59c4 (line for line, plus one removed Implements line on the deleted Process block) + proof work: XTGG/C19S, witnesses in menu-test.sh, reviews SYQB/W7QD/33/50, the impact sidecar, trace re-review stamps, the #9057 report harness and expectation, and the KI note, and the XTGG/C19S hazard reviews against catalog 1.11.0. Product-file annotations added: `// Implements: SW-REQ-261001-C19S` in finishRequest; menu-test.sh gains Verifies/mcdc:ignore header lines and one appended witness block. proof.yaml is identical to the baseline.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":144},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-test.sh","kind":"file","line":41},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-test.sh","kind":"file","line":1095}],"severity":"info","title":"Mirror composition and baseline","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}}],"packageDigest":"sha256:23944854a777d0d260b9222118f7f4f7eabf1b8454040d0acd52fb573b0de77d","packageIdentity":"epkg-853a4f00475246e7cec925e0c795b8a2d55296b1334c305dc441f48fb50b8c1f","riskAssessment":{"level":"low","rationale":"Two small changes in one function pair, each pinned by executing witnesses that fail on the previous code, 53/53 tests passing, a behaviour diff with only intended differences, and a live burst with 0 stuck callers. Not merge approval: Menu.qml has no engine-measured code MC/DC, and the 18 compatibility findings still need a reviewer."},"schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-annotation.v1","suggestedTests":[{"forClaim":5,"rationale":"Puts the reviewer's out-of-package burst result (0/20 stuck) into the evidence as an executed test.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":146}],"title":"Live 20-summon burst on b7bd59c4"},{"forClaim":6,"rationale":"Drive one bin/ caller of omarchy-menu-select, supersede it, and assert it takes its cancel path.","refs":[{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-select","kind":"file","line":96}],"title":"Superseded picker caller behaves as on Escape"},{"forClaim":7,"rationale":"Would show whether a deadline in the caller closes the remaining leg; a follow-up, not this PR.","refs":[{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-select","kind":"file","line":93}],"title":"Peer-death: bounded wait in omarchy-menu-select"}],"summary":"**What the PR does.** omacom/omarchy#9056 (FernandoJVideira; head b7bd59c4 pushed by @omarchybot) fixes #9057 in two commits. 0b4fe292: open() answers an in-flight select/input request as cancelled before the next summon replaces it. b7bd59c4: finishRequest writes every answer through Quickshell.execDetached, one process per answer, instead of the shared resultProc, so an answer issued while an earlier write runs is no longer dropped (Copilot raised this race on 2026-08-30). The resultProc Process, its redundant onExited re-close and the serial counters go. The rest of the mirror is our proof work (XTGG, C19S, witnesses, reviews, trace stamps, KI note).\n\n**Is it verified?** The audit is clean (0 errors, 0 warnings). Test results are ingested: 53/53 passed; XTGG, C19S and FGZQ are observed_pass. XTGG and C19S each have 3/4 MC/DC rows witnessed and 1 violation row excluded as defensive; the witnesses fail on the baseline and on 0b4fe292. The behaviour diff (213 inputs) finds 16 differences, all superseded or dropped callers that are now answered, none stranded, no other state change. Code-level MC/DC does not cover Menu.qml (target disabled in policy). Outside the package: live 20-summon burst 0/20 stuck on b7bd59c4 (19/20 quattro, 7-12/20 on 0b4fe292).\n\n**Questions for a human.** Approve the 18 compatibility findings (16 intended differences, the #9057 test flip, a B8N9 witness that only moved lines). Does every execDetached write start under a real burst? Do bin/ callers treat a superseded exit 1 as Escape? Peer death still strands a caller (KI stays open).\n\n**Readiness.** not_assessed until a reviewer approves the compatibility findings; policy unchanged against quattro-proof 9f3abc10. Effects were not analyzed (QML)."}
